{"name":"Debonair","hex":"#90a0a6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"debonair","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Gracious, courteous.","Suave, urbane and sophisticated."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Debonaire behaviour; graciousness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debonair"}],"entries":[{"title":"Debonair (airline)","blocks":[{"text":"Debonair was a British airline headquartered at Luton Airport offering flights to and from Spain, France, Germany and Italy. It ceased operations in October 1999 due to financial difficulties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/G-DEBA_1_146-200_Debonair_MAN_08AUG98_%286022491753%29.jpg/330px-G-DEBA_1_146-200_Debonair_MAN_08AUG98_%286022491753%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debonair_(airline)"},{"title":"Debonair (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Debonair is an English-language monthly magazine published by the Be Debonair Foundation. It is one of India's most popular entertainment magazines and includes news, interviews, photos, videos, reviews, events, and style. Previously Debonair was an Indian monthly men's magazine, originally modeled after Playboy."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a2/Debonair-india.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debonair_(magazine)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Debonair_BAe_146-200.jpg/500px-Debonair_BAe_146-200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Debonair_BAe_146-200.jpg/500px-Debonair_BAe_146-200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"British Aerospace 146 at Faro Airport in 1997","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADebonair